Subject: [PATCH 366/638] [AROS] Bootstrap Mojo invitations over native
 channels

AI_PHASE: chromium-process-model
AI_STATUS: node-controller-direct-bootstrap
ROOT_CAUSE: Mojo selected its POSIX synchronous broker bootstrap on AROS and attempted GetFD() on a native MessagePort-backed PlatformChannel.
FIX_REASON: Route AROS through NodeController's direct passed-channel invitation path, matching platforms whose bootstrap endpoint is already a complete native transport.
SCOPE: mojo/core/node_controller.cc
VALIDATION: Focused hosted invitation probe launched Process 18 and Process 29, exchanged two primordial payloads, collected child death, and exited zero in 8.11 seconds.
RISK: Full Chromium browser/renderer service binding remains the next runtime gate.
AI_DECISION_CHAIN: cross-Process Channel PASS -> invitation Broker fatal -> isolate POSIX fd assumption -> direct NodeController bootstrap -> primordial duplex PASS.
Evidence:-invitation-aros-process-20260728
Job:
